{"sectionId":"signaling/growth","items":[{"id":"signaling--growth-k001","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"mTORC1은 영양소와 성장 신호가 충분할 때 단백질 합성을 촉진하고 자가포식을 억제한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k002","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"AMPK는 에너지 부족 상태에서 활성화되어 에너지 소모성 합성 경로를 줄이고 ATP 생성 경로를 촉진한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k003","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"PI3K–Akt 신호는 TSC를 통해 mTORC1 조절에 관여한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k004","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"수용체 활성만으로 세포의 반응이 결정되는 것은 아니며 세포가 발현하는 효과기와 전사인자의 조합이 중요하다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k005","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"정형 Wnt 신호는 β-catenin의 분해를 억제하여 핵 내 전사를 조절한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k006","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"Notch는 인접 세포의 리간드에 반응하여 세포 내 도메인이 절단되고 핵으로 이동한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k007","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"Hedgehog는 Patched의 Smoothened 억제를 완화하여 Gli 조절을 바꾼다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k008","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"TGF-β 계열 수용체는 세린/트레오닌 키네이스이며 SMAD를 인산화한다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k009","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"세포자멸사에서는 미토콘드리아 cytochrome c와 Apaf-1이 caspase-9 활성화에 관여하며 죽음 수용체는 caspase-8을 활성화할 수 있다.","kind":"body-derived","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k010","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"Wnt: β-catenin; Notch: 접촉 의존성; TGF-β: SMAD.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k011","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"Bcl-2는 미토콘드리아 외막 투과화 억제에 관여하고 Bax/Bak은 촉진한다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k012","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"암 발생은 증식 신호 증가와 종양 억제 기능 소실 등이 복합적으로 작용한다.","kind":"highlight","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]},{"id":"signaling--growth-k013","sectionId":"signaling/growth","unitId":"signaling","subject":"biology","text":"mTORC1 활성은 낮아지고 자가포식은 촉진된다.","kind":"review-answer","scope":"current-scope-candidate","verificationStatus":"draft-not-independently-verified","referenceIds":["biology2e","anatomy2e"]}]}